# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the RB pack (the parked-engine rebind's slow mode; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of the integrated branch and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a
# registry: the cards are resolved at run time. Templates only: no tag is pushed by their author. ORDER.txt has the order, the stop rules, the minutes and the READ.
# ONE IMAGE: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fusion-1 is the pack's PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds (sed -i 's/tp4-fusion-1/<tag>/' *.env). The -fx-twa profiles are generated by
# make_fusion_profiles.py --write from scripts/ci/fusion-wp/RB.json on the integrated branch (WP0); until then c2_serving_job.py refuses the lever templates.
# RBA (EXACTNESS): c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-twa-audit = the production profile plus QWEN_FAST_TAP_WINDOW_ALIGNED=1 and its _AUDIT twin flag: every
# engaged window is built twice on the device (the aligned join and today's exact join of the same pieces) and compared on every chip, byte for byte.
# READ: c2_smoke_check clean with the fusion rules (an engaged line, no fell-back line, audit lines all exact=True, no mismatch), no stall, every answer complete;
# then python3 scripts/ci/rebind_split.py <container log>: 'tap window aligned: engaged=N fell_back=0 audit exact=M mismatch=0' with N > 0. ANY mismatch,
# fall-back or missing audit line is NO-GO and skips the timed jobs. Duration (estimate): 60 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fusion-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-twa-audit
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,parked_turns,concurrent8_steady
C2_BOX_MINUTES=60
